","/arc-plc/pennsylvania/luzerne-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 10 grids runs 75 years, and April to May, August to September, September to October and October to November each came in under 90% of normal in 34 of them. In 2025 on the middle of the grids, August to September came in at 48% and May to June at 171%. So far in 2026, January to February sits at 54% and March to April at 142%. Grid 25416 had its driest year in 1980 at 66%.</p>"}
